// toy guardfile - a minimal ward-kdl permission surface (exec dialect) for the
// example repo. Deny-by-default: only the read-only `status`/`list` verbs of a
// fictional `widget` CLI mount; every mutating verb falls through to the host
// deny, and the two `never` lines make that refusal explicit. This is the shape
// a consumer authors before generating a gated CLI. See ../../docs/example-repo.md
// and ../../docs/ward-kdl-authoring.md.
wrap toy widget {
    exec widget
    can run status {
        describe "show widget state (read-only)"
    }
    can run list {
        describe "list widgets (read-only)"
    }
    never run delete
    never run apply
}
